glyph-vt third-party notices
============================

`crates/glyph-vt` vendors Makepad's pure-Rust port of Ghostty's terminal
emulator core and codepoint width / UAX #29 grapheme-break library:

- `src/term/` — copied from `makepad/apps/terminal/src/term/` at makepad
  commit `7a258a35221e084fd21803a08ba4c57ab5c0b230` (omitting `key_encode.rs`
  and `mouse_encode.rs`, as `g3d-termd` encodes input on the daemon side).
- `src/cell_width/` — copied from `makepad/libs/cell_width/src/` at makepad
  commit `7a258a35221e084fd21803a08ba4c57ab5c0b230`.

Local changes to the vendored core (`src/term/`)
------------------------------------------------

1. Passive-viewer operation & bounded side buffers (`terminal.rs`):
   - Added `Terminal::with_scrollback` (used with `max_scrollback = 0` in `Vt`)
     and fixed `full_reset` (`RIS`) to preserve `max_scrollback` rather than
     reverting to `DEFAULT_SCROLLBACK` (10,000), and to clear `title` and `pwd`.
   - Added `Terminal::passive` so query replies (`outbound`) and `DCS` query
     accumulation are discarded as produced instead of growing unboundedly.
   - Converted `events` into a bounded `VecDeque<TermEvent>` (`MAX_PENDING_EVENTS = 256`)
     and added `TermEvent::ClipboardRead` (`OSC 52 ; selection ; ?`).
   - Deduplicated `OSC 8` hyperlinks via `hyperlink_ids` and added mark-and-remap
     garbage collection (`gc_hyperlinks`) plus a hard cap (`4,096` live URIs)
     and `Terminal::cell_hyperlink`.
2. `DECSTR` (`CSI ! p`, `soft_reset`) & mode parity with Ghostty (`terminal.rs`):
   - Added missing `DECSTR` resets required by `g3d-termd` repaints:
     `Wraparound`, `ReverseWrap`, `ReverseWrapExtended`, `DisableKeyboard`,
     `EnableLeftAndRightMargin` (`?69`), `CursorBlinking`, `modify_other_keys`,
     `current_hyperlink`, and resetting the 256-colour `palette` to
     `base_palette` (while preserving dynamic `OSC 10/11/12` overrides).
   - Cleared `current_hyperlink` on alternate-screen switches (`?47`/`?1047`/`?1049`)
     and cleared `SynchronizedOutput` (`?2026`) on `Terminal::resize`.
   - Tracked `mouse_tracking` (`9/1000/1002/1003`) and `mouse_format`
     (`1005/1006/1015/1016`) with xterm/Ghostty last-DECSET-wins semantics, and
     synced `Mode::CursorBlinking` on `DECSCUSR` (`CSI Ps SP q`).
3. Fuzz / edge-case hardening (`terminal.rs`, `screen.rs`, `page.rs`):
   - Fixed `Screen::resize_reflow` emitting a 3rd column (and orphan `WideTail`s)
     for every wide character by skipping old `WideTail` cells during reflow and
     regenerating tails directly beside wide heads, and degraded width-2 cells
     cleanly when reflowing onto a 1-column (`cols == 1`) grid.
   - Fixed margin-limited `Screen::scroll_up`, `Screen::scroll_down`,
     `Terminal::insert_blanks` (`ICH`), `Terminal::delete_chars` (`DCH`), and
     mode-2027 `try_grapheme_attach` (`1 <-> 2` width transitions and `cols == 1`)
     to split straddling wide characters at both boundaries and copy head style
     and hyperlink onto `WideTail`.
   - Capped per-cell grapheme cluster length (`MAX_CLUSTER_CPS = 32`) in both
     `attach_zero_width` and `try_grapheme_attach` to prevent unbounded memory
     growth and O(N^2) UAX #29 break replay on combining-mark floods; capped
     `CHT` (`CSI Ps I`) iterations to grid width.
   - Replaced potentially underflowing unsigned subtractions in `CPR` (`CSI 6 n`
     under `DECOM` when `cursor.y < scroll_top`), `CHA`/`VPA`/`CUP`,
     `cursor_left`, `erase_chars`, and `scroll_up`/`scroll_down` with saturating
     arithmetic, and removed the non-test `.unwrap()` in `Screen::resize_clamped`.
   - Added missing `dirty = true` marks on `cursor_up`, `cursor_down`,
     `cursor_right`, `cursor_left`, `carriage_return`, `horizontal_tab`,
     `horizontal_tab_back`, `restore_cursor` (default branch), `OscCommand::ChangeWindowTitle`,
     Kitty keyboard `CSI > / < / = u`, `XTMODKEYS`, and `DECKPAM`/`DECKPNM`.
4. Hot-path performance (`page.rs`, `screen.rs`, `stream.rs`, `parser.rs`, `terminal.rs`):
   - Added per-row `Row::dirty` + `Terminal::all_rows_dirty` so incremental
     `Vt::fill` skips clean rows instead of re-resolving the whole grid.
   - Recycled evicted `Row` buffers in full-width `scroll_up` / `scroll_down`
     instead of dropping and reallocating `Vec<Cell>` on every linefeed.
   - Added `Stream::process` + `Terminal::print_ascii_slice` batched ground-state
     fast path for printable ASCII runs (`0x20..=0x7e`) and direct `ESC` entry.
   - Added `Parser::step` callback dispatch (avoiding 312-byte `[Option<Action>; 3]`
     stack copies per non-ground byte) and eliminated per-SGR `Vec<Attribute>`
     heap allocation in `Terminal::apply_sgr`.

